3. Innovative Modules & Real-World Guardrails
 * 3D Drainage & Cascade Topology Twin (80/20 Leverage): Maps upstream feeders, culvert chokepoints, and downstream underpasses or sectors in 3D to test the working hypothesis that roughly 20% of drainage nodes drive about 80% of systemic flooding, showing how clearing upstream chokepoints reduces downstream flood risk.
 * 24–48 Hour Risk & Confidence Output: Combines IMD rainfall forecasts and nowcasts, sensor and CCTV signals, historical flood records, and seasonal silt data into actionable outputs—such as flagging a hotspot's risk level, confidence tier, likely upstream cause, pre-emptive action, responsible owner (e.g., Zone Junior Engineer), and target deadline.
 * Zero-PhD MCG Operations Protocol (SOPs): Operable by existing MCG staff without a dedicated data science team across T-48 to T-24h, T-24 to T-12h, T-12 to T-6h, T-6 to T-0h, During Rain, and After Rain.
 * RWA Political Economy & Transparent Dispatch Ledger: Addresses political pressure from influential RWAs by comparing objective hydrological scores against requested pump/crew shifts and logging any manual override with a documented reason across MCG and GMDA.
 * Confidence-Gated Citizen Alerts: Uses Safe, Caution, and Avoid thresholds across SMS, IVR calls (for non-smartphone users), WhatsApp/web, and corridor views, routing lower-confidence warnings to field verification first so false alarms do not erode public trust.
 * Rugged Indian-Context Hardware: Focuses on vandal-resistant, outdoor weatherproof, low-maintenance drain level gauges, rain gauges, underpass CCTV, and telemetry grounded in Indian market benchmarks.
